
# AI-Powered Customer Support & Ticket Automation System

A scalable backend application built with FastAPI, Python, PostgreSQL, SQLAlchemy, and Pydantic to manage customer support operations and automate ticket workflows using AI-powered features.

The system provides RESTful APIs for customer management, ticket handling, support agent management, ticket activity tracking, and analytics.

The project is designed to evolve into an intelligent customer support platform with automatic ticket classification, AI-generated response suggestions, and workflow automation.

## Project Overview

Customer support teams often face challenges such as:

- Managing large numbers of support requests.
- Assigning tickets to appropriate support agents.
- Tracking ticket status and priority.
- Maintaining accurate ticket activity histories.
- Monitoring support performance.
- Responding to repetitive customer questions.

This project addresses these challenges through a centralized backend system and planned AI-powered automation.

## Technology Stack

Python - Backend programming language 
FastAPI - REST API development 
PostgreSQL - Relational database 
SQLAlchemy - ORM and database operations 
Alembic -  Database migrations 
Pydantic - Request and response validation 
Uvicorn - ASGI application server 
Swagger - UI  Interactive API documentation 

## Features

### Customer Management

- Create new customers.
- Retrieve customer information.
- Update customer details.
- Delete customer records.
- Manage customer-related support tickets.

### Ticket Management

- Create support tickets.
- Retrieve ticket details.
- Update ticket information.
- Delete tickets.
- Manage ticket status and priority.
- Associate tickets with customers.

### Ticket Status Management

Supported ticket statuses:

- `open`
- `in_progress`
- `resolved`
- `closed`

Status transitions are validated to prevent unsupported workflow changes.

### Ticket Priority Management

Supported priority levels:

- `low`
- `medium`
- `high`
- `urgent`

Ticket priorities can be updated through dedicated API endpoints.

### Support Agent Management

- Create support agents.
- Retrieve agent information.
- Update agent details.
- Deactivate agents.
- Assign tickets to active agents.
- Reassign tickets between agents.
- Prevent assignment to inactive agents.

### Ticket Messages

- Add messages to support tickets.
- Retrieve ticket conversations.
- Identify message senders.

Supported sender types:

- Customer
- Support Agent
- AI

### Search, Filtering, and Pagination

Retrieve tickets using:

- Ticket status
- Ticket priority
- Customer ID
- Assigned agent ID
- Subject search

Pagination supports page numbers, result limits, total records, and navigation metadata.

### Dashboard Analytics

The backend provides ticket statistics, including:

- Total tickets
- Ticket counts by status
- Ticket counts by priority
- Ticket overview information

These APIs can support an administrative dashboard.

### Ticket Activity Logging

The system tracks important ticket events:

- Ticket creation
- Agent assignment
- Agent reassignment
- Status changes
- Priority changes

Each activity record contains:

- Ticket ID
- Activity type
- Previous value
- New value
- Performed-by information
- Timestamp

Activity history can be retrieved in chronological order.

## AI Automation Roadmap

The AI-related functionality is being developed in stages.

Planned capabilities include:

### Automatic Ticket Categorization

Automatically categorize incoming tickets into:

- Billing
- Technical
- Account
- Shipping
- Refund
- General

### AI-Based Ticket Classification

Use AI models to understand customer messages and classify support requests.

### AI Response Suggestions

Generate suggested responses to customer support questions.

### Intelligent Ticket Prioritization

Analyze customer messages to recommend appropriate ticket priorities.

### Support Workflow Automation

Automate repetitive ticket management processes and assist support agents.

